  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi></math> are three consecutive terms of a non-constant G.P. Such that the equations <math><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> have a common root, then <math><mi>&#945;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given <math><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></math> are in G.P.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#947;</mi></math><br />For the equation <math><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Hence roots of the equation are equal and equals to <math><mo>&#8211;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Since given equation have common roots, hence <math><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#947;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> must be a root of <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>.</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi></math>"
  }
